{
  "title": "Wound & Hardware Infection",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/trauma/1053/wound-and-hardware-infection",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Mar 14 2024",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Wound & Hardware Infection is the most common complication following orthopedic trauma surgery and is a significant source of patient morbidity.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be made clinically with the presence of incisional erythema, dehiscence, purulent drainage and/or persistent fracture nonunion or hardware loosening on radiographs Intraoperative deep cultures are the most reliable method to isolate causative organisms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually surgical irrigation and debridement followed by culture-directed antibiotics. Hardware removal may be performed acutely or in a delayed fashion depending on fracture healing.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**up to 16%** infection rate following traumatic fracture",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**host immunodeficiency**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "extremes of age",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "diabetes",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "obesity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "alcohol or **tobacco abuse**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "steroid use",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "malnutrition",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "medications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "previous radiation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "vascular insufficiency",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mechanisms",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "seeding",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "disruption of soft tissue envelope, blood vessels, and periosteum allow bacteria to avoid host defenses",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "direct seeding of implant and/or anatomical structure",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "hematogenous seeding",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "biofilm formation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "dependent on exopolysaccharide glycocalyx",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "history of trauma must be detailed",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "extent of soft tissue injury",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "extent of bony injury",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "previous or current hardware",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "previous or current surgery at the same site",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "history of previous skin or deep infections",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**pain at previous fracture site**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may indicate infected non-union",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "fevers, chills, and night sweats may be present",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inspection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "erythema, drainage, or **purulence**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "tenderness",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "motion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "gross motion at fracture site is suggestive of non-union",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "biplanar images of afflicted area",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "45 degree orthogonal views can also be obtained to evaluate for union",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "acute infection",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "radiographs may be normal",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "sub-acute and chronic infections",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "peri-implant lucency can be seen",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**involucrum**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1053/images/involucrum.jpg",
                          "caption": "involucrum radiograph"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "reactive bone surrounding active infection",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**sequestrum**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1053/images/sequestrum.jpg",
                          "caption": "sequestrum"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "retained nidus of infected necrotic bone",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "pre-operative planning",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "useful adjunct for diagnosis and delineating extent of disease",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "to assess soft-tissue masses and fluid collections",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "sensitivity and specificity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "98% sensitive",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "78% specific",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "WBC-labeled scans",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "can help determine infection from other similar appearing etiologies",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "helpful to detect bony infection in the setting of hardware",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "hardware can cause metal artifact in an MRI making it difficult to assess for infection",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Labs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "WBC",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may be normal in chronic or indolent infections",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "erythrocyte sedimentation rate (ESR)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may remain elevated for months following initial injury or surgery in absence of infection",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**C-reactive protein (CRP)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "most predictive for postoperative infection in the first week after fracture fixation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "should decrease from a plateau after postoperative day 2 (after fixation of fractures)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "will increase further or fail to decrease if a hematoma or infection is present",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Cultures",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "in-office cultures swabs or aspirations of wounds or sinus tracts are **unreliable**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**intraoperative deep cultures are most reliable** method of isolated causative organisms",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "multiple specimens from varying locations should be obtained",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "chronic suppression with antibiotics",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "risk of surgical treatment outweighs the benefit to the host",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "immunosuppressed, elderly, etc.",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "presence of an infected but incompletely healed fracture following internal fixation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "ESR and CRP levels used to assess adequacy of treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "32% rate of chronic infected nonunion persisting or worsening despite suppression",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "surgical debridement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "any active infection",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "hardware should be maintained if stability at risk with removal",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "low-pressure irrigation with normal saline may be superior to other methods of irrigation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "thorough identification and debridement of infection key to success",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "deep bony specimens should be obtained for culture as well as biopsy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "71% success seen with debridement and antibiotics for early acute postoperative infection",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "Risk factors for failure include intramedullary nail and open fracture",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
